# BCBA Workspace Project Rule

Before implementing or modifying code, read:

`DEVELOPMENT_DIRECTION.md`

Treat that document as the canonical project direction.

Required workflow:

1. `git status`
2. `git pull origin main`
3. confirm current commit and working tree
4. inspect relevant existing code
5. make one bounded change
6. run required verification
7. commit locally
8. push to GitHub main only when the requested task is complete

Work only in the current `bcba-workspace-ai-studio` repository unless explicitly instructed otherwise.

Do not independently reinterpret the product roadmap.
Do not duplicate existing architecture.
Do not create new persistence systems when existing `appState` supports the feature.
Do not remove legacy clinical paths without an explicit migration plan.
Do not fabricate clinical facts or automate BCBA clinical judgment.
Do not start the next roadmap item automatically.

If another instruction conflicts with `DEVELOPMENT_DIRECTION.md`, stop and identify the conflict before changing architecture.
